Why AGPL-3.0-or-later (interim stance, see LICENSE-INTENT.md):

OMEGA-64 is one of three federated substrates (omega, liquid, myc) that
together form a mycelium-style cognitive ecosystem. The substrate's value
is its position in this federation, not the engine source alone. The
AGPL-3.0-or-later license is chosen as a STOPGAP to protect that
federation from extractive forks:

  - Anyone may study, modify, and use OMEGA-64.
  - Anyone who runs a modified OMEGA-64 as a network-accessible service
    must publish their modifications (AGPLv3 §13).
  - This prevents closed proprietary forks from capturing the mycelium
    while still allowing academic study and personal research.

A custom mycelium-aware license is planned. Until it is drafted and
adopted, AGPL-3.0-or-later is the closest existing licence to that
intent.

